diff --git a/renderer/README.md b/renderer/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3d34023
--- /dev/null
+++ b/renderer/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+# smallpt in the browser
+
+Based on [Kevin Beason’s smallpt](https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/),
+Copyright 2006–2008 Kevin Beason, distributed under the MIT license in LICENSE.txt.
+The unmodified upstream source is preserved as smallpt.original.cpp.
+
+smallpt.cpp retains the original ray/sphere intersection and recursive radiance
+integrator. Its file-output main loop is replaced by an incremental RGBA API,
+seeded sampling, color setters, and an accumulation buffer. Default walls use a
+warm coral and sage palette. Every pass uses the original 2×2 subpixel layout,
+tent-filtered antialiasing, and four paths per pixel. Unlike the original's final
+subpixel clamp, this adaptation averages unclamped radiance before gamma encoding
+so additional passes converge smoothly.
+
+Run `pnpm build:wasm` with Emscripten (`emcc`) on PATH to rebuild the checked-in
+public/wasm/smallpt.js and smallpt.wasm. Run `pnpm build` to build the Astro page,
+including the static dist/client/index.html. The compiled artifacts are checked
+in so the regular web build does not require Emscripten.
+
+The browser starts a module worker, loads the WASM, and renders progressive rows
+to the canvas. Palette, quality, and resolution changes start a fresh worker.
+Pause/resume and PNG download are client-side. No rendering server is used.
+The included preview PNG is generated with this same C++ renderer and is replaced
+after the first complete browser-rendered pass.
diff --git a/renderer/smallpt.cpp b/renderer/smallpt.cpp
